<article class="env-definition" id="FC8B95">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/FC8B95">Definition <span data-tag="FC8B95">7.3.3.1</span>.</a>presheaf!with values in $\calC $ Let $X$ be a topological space, and $\calC $ an $\infty $-category. We let $\calU (X)$ denote the collection of all open subsets of $X$, partially ordered by inclusion. A <em>presheaf on $X$ with values in $\calC $</em> is a functor $\calU (X)^{op} \rightarrow \calC $. </p>
  <p>Let $\calF : \calU (X)^{op} \rightarrow \calC $ be a presheaf on $X$ with values in $\calC $. We will say that $\calF $ is a <em>sheaf</em> with values in $\calC $ if, for every $U \subseteq X$ and every covering sieve $\calU (X)_{/U}^{(0)} \subseteq \calU (X)_{/U}$, the composition </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Nerve (\calU (X)_{/U}^{(0)})^{\triangleright } \subseteq \Nerve (\calU (X)_{/U})^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \Nerve (\calU (X)) \stackrel{\calF }{\rightarrow } \calC ^{op} \]
</div>
  <p> is a colimit diagram. </p>
  <p>We let $\calP (X; \calC )$ denote the $\infty $-category $\Fun ( \calU (X)^{op}, \calC )$ consisting of all presheaves on $X$ with values in $\calC $, and $\Shv (X;\calC )$ the full subcategory of $\calP (X;\calC )$ spanned by the sheaves on $X$ with values in $\calC $. </p>
</article>